WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.434
A data type describes what kind of value Python is
working with In this module

00:00:05.645 --> 00:00:12.267
we focus on four fundamental types integer float
string and Boolean An

00:00:12.293 --> 00:00:17.506
integer is a whole number such as twelve visits A
float is a decimal number

00:00:17.769 --> 00:00:23.269
such as nineteen point ninety nine A string stores
text labels and codes

00:00:24.177 --> 00:00:29.840
A Boolean stores either true or false The type
matters because it affects

00:00:29.866 --> 00:00:36.580
which operations make sense Adding two numeric
measurements may be reasonable Adding

00:00:36.606 --> 00:00:42.461
an employee identifier to a ZIP code is not Good
analytics begins by representing

00:00:42.487 --> 00:00:44.974
each value in a way that matches its real meaning
